-canon-bookfront.charged-restraint.962073","raw_char_end":710,"raw_char_start":0,"raw_hash":"ab5df71d07941f10a7162ba53116c0f375e0bb01d6786fca9bbfd262d5518bb4","raw_path":"03_scene_lab/runs/prompt-autoresearch-v27-single-mode-source/runways/raw/runway.graph-paired-canon-bookfront.charged-restraint.962073.txt","role":"opening-runway","span_id":"runway.graph-paired-canon-bookfront.charged-restraint.962073","text_hash":"3e5ba8ede750239fc5b3d56ef0005e82e0e746b743a280d694a59c818e998537"},"status":"completed","text":"After a late lab session, Jonah and I walk out into an unfamiliar evening. We have each felt the air change but not yet found the words for it. We breathe quietly as the temperature cools around us. He has the keys so we wait for each other in the dark parking lot until the exit door opens with a clunk. The late session is over and no one wants to talk.\n\nAs we walk toward his parked car, he does not speak, nor I to him. A few weeks ago, we would have filled this space with silence or inane chitchat. Instead we let the silence fall over us like a blanket, and I can't say if he's thinking the same thing. I'm thinking he might kiss me, and when that thought is over I'm thinking no, I'm not thinking that.","text_hash":"3e5ba8ede750239fc5b3d56ef0005e82e0e746b743a280d694a59c818e998537","timings":{"cache_n":1475,"predicted_ms":21515.731,"predicted_n":240,"predicted_per_second":11.154629140883014,"predicted_per_token_ms":89.64887916666666,"prompt_ms":86.484,"prompt_n":1,"prompt_per_second":11.562832431432405,"prompt_per_token_ms":86.484},"usage":{"completion_tokens":240,"prompt_tokens":1476},"version":"gemma-fiction-autoresearch.v4"}
